## Orchestrator Directors (free-text entry points)

This `.cursorrules` is **automatically aware** of all three frameworks and their directors. The full framework topology is hardcoded below — no additional config needed.

| Director | Framework | Purpose | Invocation |
|----------|-----------|---------|------------|
| `@ai-director` | `.ai/` (Agent OS) | Engineering: planning, coding, DB, dev stack, sessions | `@ai-director - <describe what you want>` |
| `@ui-director` | `/mnt/work/Projects/.ai.ui/` (UI Design OS) | UI: design tokens, screen specs, components, visual/a11y verify | `@ui-director - <describe what you want>` |
| `@biz-director` | `/mnt/work/Projects/.ai.biz/` (Business OS) | Business: strategy, brand, content, sales, pricing | `@biz-director - <describe what you want>` |
| `@x-director` | Cross-framework | Coordinates across ≥2 of `.ai` / `.ai.ui` / `.ai.biz` | `@x-director - <describe what you want>` |

**Skill files:** `.ai/skills/ai-director/skill.md` · `.ai/skills/x-director/skill.md` · `/mnt/work/Projects/.ai.ui/skills/ui-director/skill.md` · `/mnt/work/Projects/.ai.biz/skills/biz-director/skill.md`

### Routing rules

Free-text requests are routed by intent:

```
Free-text request
       │
       ├── Engineering only ──────────► @ai-director - <request>
       │
       ├── UI only ────────────────────► @ui-director - <request>
       │
       ├── Business only ──────────────► @biz-director - <request>
       │
       ├── Cross-framework ────────────► @x-director - <request>
       │     (spans ≥2 of: .ai / .ai.ui / .ai.biz)
       │
       └── Unsure / underspecified ───► @x-director - <request>
```

- `@x-director` classifies intent, determines dependency order (e.g. API before UI), and invokes each framework's director sequentially.
- Do not bypass directors by invoking framework-specific skills directly.
- Do not reimplement another framework's skills inside `.ai/`.

