## Documentation layout (`.ai/` vs `.work/`)

**`.ai/`** — agnostic: skills, standards, concepts, workflow guides, integration mirror, `START_HERE.md`, `PROCESS_ROUTER.md`, **`templates/`** (including this file's source). Pointer READMEs only under `.ai/plans/`, `.ai/features/`, etc.

**`.work/`** — project-specific: plans, SPECs, ADRs, prompts, `HANDOFF.md`.

Generated filenames under `.work/` use the `YYYYMMDD-` prefix unless documented otherwise (`NEXT.md`, `HANDOFF.md`, …).

| Path | Layer |
|------|-------|
| `.work/plans/` | Plans, registries, `NEXT.md` |
| `.work/features/` | Feature SPECs |
| `.work/decisions/` | ADRs |
| `.work/prompts/` | Questionnaires; user scratch |
| `.work/context/HANDOFF.md` | Session handoff |
| `.ai/standards/` | Binding engineering standards |
| `.ai/skills/` | Portable agent skills |
| `.ai/templates/cursorrules.template` | **Copy to repo root as `.cursorrules`** when bootstrapping |

Canonical map: `.ai/README.md` · Working tree: `.work/README.md`.

