### UI skills (`@ui-*` only)

| Skill | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| ui-bootstrap | `.work.ui/` + cursorrules merge |
| ui-design-foundation | Foundation 01–04; screen-spec-ready |
| ui-screen-spec | `.work.ui/screens/` SPECs |
| ui-component-build | `NEXT_UI.md` iterations |
| ui-visual-verify | Visual regression |
| ui-accessibility-audit | WCAG |
| ui-design-system | Catalog + Storybook |
| ui-concept-run | UIS-01…07 |
| ui-process-router | UI Q&A (read-only) |

**Sessions:** `@session-control` (`.ai/`) · **Backend:** `@code-implementation` (`.ai/`) · **UIS-06** + **UIS-07** (tier ≥ refined) before `ui-component-build complete`.

### UI protected files (union with existing list)

- `web/src/app/globals.css` (token file)
- `web/next.config.ts`, `web/tsconfig.json` (framework config)
- `/mnt/work/Projects/.ai.ui/inputs/brand/` (reference — do not auto-edit)

### UI Design & implementation discipline

- No raw `#RRGGBB` or magic spacing in feature components — use `web/src/app/globals.css` tokens.
- New primitives via `@ui-design-system add` with coverage.
- Screen work requires an **Approved** screen SPEC before `@ui-component-build start`.
- Target: WCAG AA. Focus visible; labels on controls; `prefers-reduced-motion` honored.
- Avoid generic AI chrome (gradient heroes, inconsistent radii) unless SPEC requests it.

